id: rust.ownership-move
kind: rust
title: Ownership and moves in server code
aliases: ownership, move semantics, borrow checker
tags: ownership, fundamentals
questions:
  - why does the compiler say my value was moved?
invariant: One owner per value; passing by value moves it, borrowing is a loan the compiler tracks.
answer_30s: Moves are the default for non-Copy types, so a value handed to a task or struct is no longer yours; clones and references are deliberate alternatives.
when_to_use:
  - struct and function signatures, deciding clone versus borrow versus take
failure_modes:
  - cloning a large payload per request to satisfy the borrow checker
  - moving a value into a spawned task and then trying to use it afterwards
related:
  - rust.borrow-lifetimes
  - rust.arc
  - rust.tokio-spawn
sources:
  - https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch04-00-understanding-ownership.html
